  "body": "`scan::binaries` lists `tests/*.rs` only, and the quick tier treats a changed `tests/<dir>/x.rs` as shared input and runs every suite of the crate. So test files cannot be folded into fewer binaries (app has 268; 133 of them hold five tests or fewer) without losing the quick tier's changed-test selection. Teach `scan`, `quick` and `gate test` to list, select and run a directory suite and its changed test functions.\n\nProcess files (xtask): bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`.\n\nDone means: a directory suite is listed, selected by a change to one of its files (only that suite, only the changed test fns where quick does that today), and runnable by name with `gate test`; pinned by xtask unit tests. Prerequisite for folding test binaries (#919 question 3).\n\nLists, counts and evidence: the research comment on #919 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-6808141599).\n\nPart of #919.\n",
